  "question": {
    "text": "The kinetic study of a reaction like $v A \\rightarrow P$ at $300 \\mathrm{K}$ provides the following curve, where concentration is taken in mol $\\mathrm{dm}^{-3}$ and time in min.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2019_che_q72.png\">\r\nIdentify the correct order $(n)$ and rate constant $(k)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2lSlj",
      "text": "$n=0, k=4.0 \\mathrm{mol} \\mathrm{dm}^{-3} \\mathrm{min}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0jcS4",
      "text": "$n=1 / 2, k=2.0 \\mathrm{mol}^{1 / 2} \\mathrm{dm}^{-3 / 2} \\mathrm{min}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xroaP",
      "text": "$n=1, k=80 \\mathrm{min}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d0ezx",
      "text": "$n=2, k=16.0 \\mathrm{dm}^{3} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1} \\mathrm{min}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From the given graph Slope $=\\frac{(\\text { rate })^{1 / 2}}{[A]}=4$\r\n$\\because$ rate $(r)=k[A]^{n}$\r\nWhere, $k=$ rate constant $[A]=$ concentration at time $t$ (in min).\r\n$n=$ order.\r\nAccording to the graph $(n=2)$ $\\therefore \\quad k=\\frac{\\text { rate }}{[A]^{n}}=[4]^{2}=16$\r\nHence, $n=2$ and\r\n$$\r\nk=16.0 \\mathrm{dm}^{3} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1} \\min^{-1}\r\n$$\r\nand option (d) is the correct answer.",
    "image": null
  },
